web search: https://cvsweb.netbsd.org/bsdweb.cgi/src/sys/arch/alpha/pci/lca_pci.c?rev=HEAD&content-type=text/x-cvsweb-markup
codex
The hardware manual confirms that `IOC_CONF` supplies the configuration-cycle type bits. The type-1 bus number comes from the address, so the fix needs a bus decode as well as your device decode. The existing witness also has a zero bus field in its tag; setting `IOC_CONF` to 1 does not make that a bus-1 address.
