There is another premise to correct: the LCA manual specifies arbitrary read data plus an exception and logged error when no device responds. All-ones is therefore an emulator compatibility result here, not a complete hardware contract. Also, a literal `return 0` differs from a successful zero-filled return: Alpha’s load path can leave the destination register unchanged, which matters because the witness reuses its control-read register.
